::Q1::In ETL, when does transformation occur? 
{
~Only after all data has been queried
~Transformation never occurs in ETL
=Before the transformed data is loaded into the warehouse
~After the warehouse has served the final report
}

::Q2::What is the Extract step responsible for? 
{
=Pulling raw data from source systems
~Creating dimension tables from scratch without source data
~Writing final reports for business users
~Deleting the source database
}

::Q3::What is the Load step in ETL? 
{
=Writing the transformed data into the destination warehouse
~Cleaning data before extraction
~Pulling raw data from the source
~Running a report against the source system
}

::Q4::Why did ELT become more practical with modern cloud data warehouses? 
{
~Cloud warehouses cannot store raw data
~Cloud platforms only support manual transformations
~Modern warehouses removed the need for extraction
=Modern warehouses have enough processing power to perform large-scale transformations directly
}

::Q5::Which sequence correctly represents ELT? 
{
~Transform → Extract → Load
=Extract → Load → Transform
~Load → Extract → Transform
~Extract → Transform → Load
}